From 15bdb88a085ac1699548d0767b139362f36728ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slopdealer <326519127+slopdealer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 14:28:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/49] R9: a wrong password that needs no prompt costs one key
 search, as in stock

After a failed search over the staged key listing the whole search was run
again: with a wrong RESTIC_PASSWORD every key file was loaded and derived
twice before the same error (20 keys: 40 scrypt derivations).

The second search exists for a staged listing that is no longer current and
for a key load that failed. It now first takes its ordinary key listing and
compares it with the keys the first search read and rejected. When the
first search ended with "no key found" or "maximum number of keys reached",
none of its loads failed and the repository still has exactly these keys,
the second search would repeat every derivation with the same result: it is
ended before its first key and the first error is returned. Any other case
is searched again as before, over the listing just taken.

Two league tests asserted the doubled work and are corrected:
TestOpeningActualPathsMatchOrdinary/wrong (40 key loads against 20) and
TestB01OpeningConfigFailureMatrix (2 key loads against 1).

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
